# playpick: mode=daily boss=gorged (coverage label only -- a daily's boss
# comes off the UTC date, not a pickable control) spec=priest:shadow
# style=wander view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# Probed first (2026-09-27-8-probe.play): today's actual daily is The Three
# Crowns again, but not the same instance as any prior session this line has
# logged -- every prior Crowns daily was 25-player normal/SWARMING; this one
# is 25-player HEROIC with HASTENED ("the enrage arrives more than two
# minutes early"). direction.md's own note on this fight names wander and
# dodge as the only two vocabulary styles it had never seen; dodge got its
# pull on 2026-09-27 (mode=raid, 10-normal) and read byMechanic={} because
# dodge has no toward-boss term at all, so it never walks onto the untouchable
# decoy the way melee/good do. wander is different again: it presses a random
# ability slot round-robin AND picks a new random heading every twelve steps,
# so unlike dodge it has no reason to avoid the court either -- this is the
# first style with genuinely undirected movement to meet this fight, and the
# first time this fight's hastened-enrage variant has been played by anyone.
